Z||000000||Galen||07-27-2001||12:28 AM||||As I start this rant, I wanna say I'm American. So forgive me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>People complain about being treated equal. Thats a noble thought that if we all could treat everyone with equal respect and such, it would be a wonderful world. I say not true. For example, if a man(or a woman) comes up to you and slaps you. To show that man equal respect you would be required to slap him back. But wait, thats assualt. Bad idea. <P>And now jumping full circle, or only half circle, Thats up to you. A man who is disabled, wishs to be treated the same as a man that is not disabled. Yet you go to Wal-Mart(yes I'm partial) on a busy day. The parking lot is full, you have no where to park. You must spend time, wasting your gas that you spent hardearned money on trying to find a parking place. However, this man who is disabled, who wishes to be treated equally, has a parking place up front that is reserved. He does not have to hunt for a parking place, he does not have to waste his gas, that he paid for with money that was earned on a job that is easy to do. Does this sound like we are treating him equally? <P>The following may piss a few women off, if so oh well. Women wish to be treated equally as well. They say they can do any job a man can do. Okie, no problems there with me, IF they can do it. I recently read a article on a friends website about his workplace, (<A HREF="http://www.slackersguild.com/article.pl?sid=01/07/18/0040243" TARGET=_blank>click here</A>), in which he works with a female as a equal coworker. Yet, in his eyes, she is treated equal to him. Until it is time for the two of them to do equal work. Then it all goes out the door, he does the work, She helps. Not THEY do the work and not SHE does the work and he helps. Wheres the equality there?<P>All things being said, equality in the world is a noble thought yes. And if it was done correctly, would make some people happy, and some people unhappy. Should I lose a job, for the simple fact that the place I work has a lack of minority in their workforce? When I am more capable of doing the job than someone else? Its your world, you decide.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"It may be the opinion of the court, but its still wrong"</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/download.html" TARGET=_blank>Download FieroProject.com Chat Client v1.50 Today</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||AkursedX||07-27-2001||12:45 AM||||You bring up some very interesting points in your little rant.  And for the most part I agree with you.  <P>I just basically want to say that there is no way everyone on this planet is going to be happy.  There are too many differences in people to please everyone.  <P>So you can do one of two things.  You can A) complain about all the problems in this world or B) You can shut up and deal with it.  <P>But there is no "correct" answer for everyone.  I choose to shut up and deal with it.  I have enough stuff in my life to worry about.  I don't need to worry about things I can't change.  But, that is what is right for me.  It might not be the right thing for someone else though.  We are all different.<P>And don't take this as a flame Galen, because it's not.  Not that I think you would car anyways  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Live and Learn......<P><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DecadenceR||07-27-2001||01:15 AM||||I often think of the same type of things. I a not racist by any means. But if 1000 white men gather, it's a racist meeting. 1000 black men gather, it's a rally for racial unity. Black people blame white people for the mistakes and wrong doings of people that have been dead for over 100 years. Women want to earn as much as men, but most are not willing to do any of the dangerous jobs. Young people want the right to drink and do things that are reserved for adults, but are not willing to take the responsibility for those things. they think their parents will fix it. We are not allowed to own land in Japan, I believe it is. Yet, who owns a VERY large part of our land and corporations in the US? we see it all the time everywhere we go. Turn on a TV, what are the first words you hear? "WHITE cop shoots BLACK man in robbery attempt.." Who cares what color who was? Someone was robbing, and someone was doing whatthey were trained to do. And anyone that wants equal rights wants the right to march, vote, own, earn, and things of the such. but when it's time to go to war or fight or stand up for those rights everyone wanted so bad, the people that were the loudest in the fight for them are now the meekest of the lot.<BR>Total equality is a pipe dream. There will always be at least one person that wants more, or thinks they deserve more, than all the rest.<p>[This message has been edited by DecadenceR (edited 07-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Galen||07-27-2001||03:41 AM||||"White cop shoots black man in robbery attempt"... most the time the news distorts the fact that, BLACK man was breaking the law, WHITE cop was doing his job. If the roles were reversed, would it make the news? Doubtful, Just like the man who shot two students, it made the news for just one student. Cuz he was gay. Yup, shooting a gay guy is a hate crime, put it everywhere on the news. Shooting a straight guy, Oh it was just another murder.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"It may be the opinion of the court, but its still wrong"</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/download.html" TARGET=_blank>Download FieroProject.com Chat Client v1.50 Today</A>||||reg||1
