Z||000005||Songman||07-27-2001||08:15 PM||||I'm going to quote a little bit from Lewis Grizzard since I agree with almost everything he says... not all, but almost...<P>He talks about the Rodney King verdict. A quote from a white man on the news cast the night of the verdict. "I was so upset by the verdict that I went downtown, knocked a window out of Brooks Brothers and stole a couple of suits. Made me feel much less irate."<P>He went on to say "I don't understand these looters. Why are these people burning their own neighborhoods and killing their own people if they're so mad about the Rodney King verdict? It would have made more sense to go over to Rodeo Drive and burn and loot there. It's like somebody shooting me in the foot and me deciding to shoot myself in the other foot to get even. I saw many photographs in the newspapers during the riots showing looters. One showed women stealing clothes out of a clothing store. The women were all smiling. If they were than angry over the Rodney King verdict, why were they smiling? What has committing a felony and smiling while doing it got to do with rage against the Justice system?"<P>Now I am speaking for me again... Everyong knows I tend to stand up for rights.. everyone's rights! But as a SSWM, as called by Grizzard (Single Southern White Male), I am the most targeted for having my rights taken away. Everyone gets all offended by off-color remarks about whatever race they happen to be in, but everyone gets a kick out of bubba or redneck jokes.<P>I don't have quotas guaranteeing me a job, I don't have special foundations trying to guarantee me a college education, I can't say that someone is discriminating against me every time I don't get my way, I don't get John F. Kennedy Day off from work, I can't go watch the Miss White America pageant, I can't watch White Entertainment Television, I can't celebrate Confederate History Month.. the list is endless!<P>But the thing is, I don't expect or even want all of these things. I just want people to be people. I don't dislike blacks, whites, yellows, reds, Protestant, Catholic, Jewish, Buddhist, Americam, Canadian, European, African, male, female... you get my point? I treat everyone as an individual and they will either gain my respect, ire, or just indifference individually. But the people who want something special over what the rest of us get, those people are not winning the vote with me.<P>I don't know about other countries.. Do ya'll have African-Canadians, or African-French, or African-Mexicans or is that something that is just saved for us awful Americans. I've already said before. My ancestors many generations back came from Scotland but I am not Scottish-American. I am American. And as long as people want special treatment for no other reason than they can be annoying enough and eventually get it, you are right.. we will never have equality. But people need to quit blaming it on the SSWM's of the world and put the blame where it belongs...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Galen||07-29-2001||08:38 AM||||in all realism, I do believe songman posted just to show his was bigger than mine.<P>hehe.. and he did it without going to a field  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"And God said there shall be one in thy owns image, and he made me"</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/download.html" TARGET=_blank>Download FieroProject.com Chat Client v1.50 Today</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Stage-2GT||07-29-2001||09:26 AM||||  It's the same old song and dance, everyone want's something for nothing. That's a very generalized statement. Some points made are correct and some are rather ambiguous. <BR>  Let's start by saying, lables, weather race or gender related, are meer tools used to gain advantage. By saying you are a black man of a female you have hiring priority. You have to, if not, someone is in trouble. At the same, time you cannot be harrassed for not doing the same work as others. If you feel, as a black man or a woman, that you are being harrassed, no questions asked, someone will be in trouble.<BR>  Songman, your into C/W, you tell me why in the pas ten years that there has been such an influx of Female C/W artists. Is it because they are really that good? I don't think so. It's because of the one phrase that will destroy us all, "Political Correctness". If you don't give these women a chance, a chance you wouldn't give to comparable male artist, you will be in trouble. <BR>  This whole problem is based in political correctness. It's about what looks good for the politicians. Do you think the ploticians really care about the women, or the ethnic people? Hell no! They exploit these groups for their own agenda and further the decay the fabric of our society. How many politicians do you think go to capital hill and speak the voice of their constituency? NONE! They arrive in their respective state and federal seats with their own agenda. They pander the vote of the public and then turn their backs on the very people who got them there. Yet any time they feel threatened, they throw some meaningless carrot out there to those same mindless dolts and are granted forgiveness.<BR>  Now, let's break it down a bit more. Who do you think hold the resposibility for those politicians that hold office? We do! We are the ones who vote them in and when they stop listening to us, we do nothing. Most of us do not even vote, we don't want to waste our happy hour to be in a polling station. Yet we will sit and complain about the results after the fact. It is us as individuals who are resposible for these problems because we won't voice our opinions and distaste for these actions. IF you want things to change or even the smallest chance of change, you have to get proactive. If you can't see your self as being proactive, then just shut up! I hope like hell that their are some proactive folks hear.<P>S2GT <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>"If Hate Was Money, I Would Own The World"||||reg||9
