Z||000016||Stage-2GT||07-30-2001||08:10 PM||||  Boy, that's the pot calling the kettle black! Galen, you have no idea what the world is about do you? It has to stop somewhere or it's all going to end in a heap. Your elected officials would sell you down the river (and pretty much are) if they thought that there would be a gross profit in it for them. Did you hear the latest? Now, if you collect Social Security and earn $30,000 in other retirement income, your Social Security, that you MUST pay into, will be taxed 40%. If you are married and earn a combined income of $40,000 your SS will be taxed at 85%. Now, I don't recall anyone ever running that one by us, do you? and if they did, do you think the public would feel that acceptable. Also, where will all that money saved go? Hum, perhaps into some congressional slush fund to be squandered like the rest of the SS money has been. I don't consider political oversight childish at all. As a matter of fact it is a right and responsibility of every citizen to ensure that the government operates within it's bounds. Problem is, people would rather be told what to do than make, or help make the important decisions. People are happy to get what ever they get as long as they don't have to be bothered. Welcome to America, where the people (or most of them anyway) are like sheep, ready to do what you tell them to, without question. No thank you!!<P>S2GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>------------------<BR>"If Hate Was Money, I Would Own The World"<p>[This message has been edited by Stage-2GT (edited 07-31-2001).]||||reg||13
